# ---------------------------------------------------------------- RouteWatch
#
# Two categories are deliberately kept out of the repository.
#
# 1. CACHED API CONTENT
#    AeroDataBox Terms of Use, Article 5.5, caps cached Contents at seven days,
#    and 5.2(g) forbids building a permanent database out of them. A file that is
#    committed lives in git history forever, which is the opposite of a cache.
#    RouteWatch reads these CSVs on every run and keeps only its own computed
#    results, so nothing of value is lost by not committing them.
#
# 2. THE IMMERSION VARIANT - permission granted 19 August 2026
#    docs/community-immersion.json carries flight numbers, departure times and
#    airline per route. AeroDataBox has confirmed that the Plan Terms permit
#    showing those fields to end users (Articles 5.6 and 5.3), so the docs/ path
#    is no longer ignored and GitHub Pages may serve it.
#
#    The data/ path stays ignored. Setting IMMERSION_DIR=data is the private
#    fallback, and a private copy has no reason to sit in git history.
#
#    Two things did NOT change with the permission:
#      - aircraft registrations are still excluded from the variant, by the script
#      - the seven-day cache rule below still applies to raw CSVs

# Cached API responses, seven-day retention
data/manual/*.csv

# Private fallback location for the flight-level variant
data/community-immersion.json

# Local scanner output: describes one person's machine, not the project
data/sim-scan.json
data/sim-scan.md
data/xplane-scan.json
data/xplane-scan.md
config/collection.scan.json

# Reports regenerated on every run
data/retention-check.md
data/variant-comparison.md

# Local noise
node_modules/
.DS_Store
.env
*.log
